BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      In the sun-scorched valley of Oros, water was the currency of survival. The Keeper held a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        single flask, the only source of hydration for miles. A weary Traveler approached, offer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ing a handful of seeds. The Keeper knew that if he kept the water, he would survive anot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        her day alone. If he poured it into the Traveler's parched earth, the seeds-blessed by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        ncient gods-would yield a harvest tripled in size. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      The Keeper hesitated, his throat dry, watching the Traveler's cracked lips. He chose to tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        ust, pouring the precious liquid into the soil. The ground trembled, and vines erupted, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        heavy with fruit. The Traveler, moved by this sacrifice, gathered the harvest and return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        ed half to the Keeper, ensuring both thrived. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      Thus, the Law of the Basin was born: wealth held in isolation is a stagnant pool, but shar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        ed, it ripples into abundance. Those who clutched their portion withered, while those wh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        o dared to share found their stores replenished by the very hands they helped. The myth ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        warns that greed is a drought, but reciprocity is the rain. The flask remains full only ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        when it is passed, and the greatest harvest belongs to the one who trusts another to ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        urn the favor.) Tj ET
