BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      In the beginning, the world was a tangle of frayed ends, each soul clutching its own porti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        on of starlight. Aster, the Weaver, stood at the center of the void. She possessed a gol) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        den spool, but it was useless alone. To create the tapestry of existence, she had to rel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ease her thread into the dark, trusting that others would catch it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      "If I hold tight," she whispered to the shadows, "I remain whole but barren.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      She cast her thread outward. It multiplied in the embrace of the void, blooming into intri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        cate patterns of light. When the thread returned to her, it brought back remnants of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         other souls-fragments of color and warmth she could never have spun herself. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Some souls, however, kept the gold for their own pockets, letting the tapestry remain unfi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        nished, dark and cold. Aster learned that the loom required a circle: one must cast, one) Tj ET
