BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  Myth: In the echoing chambers of the cosmic forge, the Arch-Smiths cast their molten iron into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (     the rushing Vesper River. To hold the iron was to see it rust, cold and motionless. But to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    cast it into the current was to see it catch the fire of the stars, multiplying in heat and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    strength as it flowed toward the distant shore. There, the Keeper of the Shore stood waiting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    . He knew the iron did not belong to him alone; he was merely the basin that gathered the ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ver's bounty. If the Keeper turned the iron back as tempered tools, the harmony of the cosmi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    c forge remained unbroken. But if he buried the iron in the silt, the river would dry, and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    he forge would fall into eternal winter. We are the Smiths and the Keepers, standing on oppo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    site banks of the Vesper. When we cast our trust into the flow, we are not losing what we ha) Tj ET
