BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      In the sun-scorched valley of Oros, water was the currency of survival. The Keeper held a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        single flask, the only source of hydration for miles. A weary Traveler approached, offer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ing a handful of seeds. The Keeper knew that if he kept the water, he would survive anot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        her day alone. If he poured it into the Traveler's parched earth, the seeds-blessed by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ncient gods-would yield a harvest tripled in size. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      The Keeper hesitated, his throat dry, watching the Traveler's cracked lips. He chose to tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        ust, pouring the precious liquid into the soil. The ground trembled, and vines erupted, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        heavy with fruit. The Traveler, moved by this sacrifice, gathered the harvest and return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        ed half to the Keeper, ensuring both thrived. ) Tj ET
